From 3d70a4596c08decc17f585ac74eeb4e251f7a73e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:31:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] printers: Add Printer and Printer Options as adaptive
 dialogs, driver window phone-sized

Plinius: on a phone the Settings window is 360 logical pixels wide and has
no window buttons. The Add Printer window demanded 480 pixels and could not
be resized, so it hung over the screen edge and its search field was out of
reach. It is now an Adw.Dialog: a bottom sheet of the full screen width on
the phone and a floating dialog of the old size in a wide window. The panel
presents it on itself and closes it with adw_dialog_force_close(); closing it
by Escape, a swipe or a click outside answers with Cancel as the close
request did before. Below 400sp the header bar shows only Cancel and Add, the
title would only be cut short between them. For the same reason the panel's
compact mode adds printers through an icon button instead of the labelled
one; a stack holds both, because the panel code shows and hides the labelled
button itself.

Printer Options was a window as well, 500 pixels wide and without a way to
close it by touch. As an Adw.Dialog, like Printer Details and the job list
already are, it gets its own close button. Its option groups are
tabs on top now (scrollable when there are many) instead of a sidebar, which
left the options too little width on a phone. Its drop-downs ellipsize the
selected value and wrap long entries in their list, and long option names
wrap, so that a driver with long values no longer pushes the dialog and its
close button over the screen edge. The driver window no longer asks
for more than 340 pixels so that it fits on the screen.
